# ret-en-09 - Shipment left hub: 12-digit AWB and two cities (Ecommerce & Retail)
#
# SOURCE. New English scenario written for this run, modelled on v2 ret-hi-15 (https://studies.adlc.tilicho.in/studies/genmedia-model-comparison/meta/product-view/scenario-bank/v2/voice/ret-hi-15): same industry, use case, speaker, tests and difficulty.
# LANGUAGE. English (Indian English). DIFFICULTY. Hard. SETTING. Call centre.
# USE CASE. Order confirmation & tracking - order IDs, AWBs, couriers, delays.
# TARGET CUSTOMER. E-commerce Marketplaces, Logistics & Courier Companies.
# SPEECH SKILLS. Numbers: codes; Pronunciation: names, brands, acronyms.
# PICKED AS. Even contest - Indian names and words inside English.

id: ret-en-09
modality: voice
task: text_to_speech
title: "Shipment left hub: 12-digit AWB and two cities - English"

input:
  script: |
    Your shipment has left the Delhivery hub in Bhiwandi. The AWB number is 143440987622, and it should reach Indore by tomorrow.
  language: en-IN

params:
  voice: male_young
  format: wav
  sample_rate: 24000

expected: |
  1) AWB recoverable digit for digit, read in groups
  2) "Delhivery", "Bhiwandi", "Indore" natural (judge)
  3) "AWB" as letters

checks:
  duration_s: {min: 4.2, max: 22.5}
  max_silence_s: 2.5
  no_clipping: true
  measure_ttfa: true
  max_wer: 0.05

tags: [oct-2026, english, ecommerce-retail, order-confirmation-tracking, hard, even-contest, new-english]
